Audit complete: **CONCERNS / LEGIT**.

The proof reconstructs successfully, pins the submitted program, covers the unrestricted contract domain, and rejects both body and postcondition mutations. The concern is that three low-level return/scope normalization bridges lack successful bridge-free universal proofs due to Haskell backend normalization gaps; static and concrete evidence supports their soundness.

